# VIDEO-mode KEY frame byte-identity matrix, 72x88 q40 — AFTER wiring the
# video arm's SPATIAL SSE at MDS1 (docs/INTER-ENCODE-PLAN.md §1o''')

date: 2026-09-01
host: mac (Apple aarch64, M-series), release build
base: dbf067070190 (the video-arm loop-restoration ladders, 57/60)

## How it was produced

  tools/video_key_matrix.sh <outdir>

72x88 q40, five synthetic content classes x twelve presets, frames=2
low-delay-P, FRAME 0 compared.

## Result

**58 / 60 byte-identical**, up from 57.

Closed: `diag p0` (C 207 B; port 206 -> 207).
Unchanged: `screenrep p0` at 0.043 %.
MOVED THE WRONG WAY IN BYTES: `gradient p0` 0.447 % -> 0.522 % (port 1335 ->
1348 against C's 1341 — it crossed over C). Recorded, not hidden: on the
64-aligned cell this chunk was localized on (`gradient 128x128 q40 p0`) the
SAME change took the coded tree from 287 field flips to 201 with `bsize` and
`txd` flips going to ZERO and port-only geometry to ZERO, and made every MDS1
candidate's distortion equal C's. The byte count is not the thing improving
here; §1f's cancellation warning applies in both directions.

The chunk's own cell, on a geometry with no partial superblocks:
`gradient 128x128 q40 p2` C 3257 / port 3257 with DIFFERING bytes ->
byte-identical. p0 2714 -> 2651 (C 2665), p1 2961 -> 2990 (C 3012).

## Read the verdict column, not the percentage

A zero percentage is a SIZE claim, not a byte claim (§1i). `gradient 128x128
q40 p2` above is the live example: 3257 on both sides, 0.000 %, and NOT
byte-identical before this chunk.

## A SECOND geometry, same build: 128x128

`VKM_W=128 VKM_H=128 tools/video_key_matrix.sh` —
`benchmarks/video_key_matrix_128x128_2026-09-01-ssse.tsv`. Also **58 / 60**,
and the two open cells are the SAME two content classes at the SAME preset:
`gradient p0` (C 2665, port 2651, 0.525 %) and `screenrep p0` (C 6517, port
6518, 0.015 %). 128x128 has FOUR COMPLETE superblocks and no partial-SB
geometry at all, so the residual is a content x preset property, not an
alignment one — which is why §1o''' localizes on this geometry rather than on
72x88.

## Cross-ISA

Re-run on x86-64 (`r7900x`, Ryzen 9 7900X, Linux) at commit 4ab2288c6665 from a
scratch clone: **58 / 60 on BOTH geometries**, cell for cell the same verdicts
as aarch64, with `cargo nextest run --workspace` 2428/2428 and
`tools/regression_spotcheck.sh` 64/64.
